  "body": "Orthographic (parallel) viewport projection, issue #434.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `Camera` grows a `projection: ProjectionMode` field; `Perspective` stays\n  the default. The mode rides the camera itself, so `mvp`, `ray_through`\n  and `dolly_cursor` share one decision by construction and every existing\n  `mvp(aspect)` call site keeps working untouched. `frame`, `toward` and\n  `oriented` carry it; orbit, pan and zoom leave it alone.\n- Ortho branch: an affine matrix (clip.w is 1, linear depth), view\n  half-height `dist * tan(30 deg)` - exactly the height perspective sees\n  at the target plane - so the mode switch never jumps the framing and\n  `dist` keeps spelling zoom for orbit, pan and frame alike. Pick rays go\n  parallel through the same matrix, and the ortho dolly holds the world\n  point under the cursor.\n- Ephemeral view state, like the Solids radios: a direct field flip\n  through `actions::toggle_projection`, never a command, never saved in\n  the project; the sim's `PreviewCamera` stays perspective.\n- UI: a Projection radio row (Perspective / Ortho) under the Solids radios\n  in the browser pane, and bare P in `shortcuts()` toggles it with the\n  same guard as bare F, so Ctrl+P keeps its post dialog and the Alt lanes\n  stay clear.\n\n**Pinned by**\n\n`projection_tests` in `crates/ui/src/law_tests.rs`: the ortho matrix is\naffine where perspective is not, ortho rays are parallel (and distinct\nrays for distinct cursors) and the cursor closes through the matrix,\nsizes ignore depth where perspective shrinks them, the mode switch agrees\nat the target plane, the ortho dolly holds the cursor point, and the\ncamera transforms carry the mode. In the egui shell:\n`projection_radios_flip_the_viewport_mode` (real pointer events, queues\nnothing) and `bare_p_flips_projection_without_a_command` (P toggles,\nCtrl+P still arms the post dialog). Snapshots rebuilt for the new\nbrowser row.\n\n**Not exercised**\n\n- No live GPU interaction test for the new pick path beyond the CPU\n  matrix closure (`projection_tests`): the wgpu renderer just consumes the\n  same `mvp` matrix, so the draw side rides existing `gpu_render` lanes.\n- The sim's `PreviewCamera` (and trace.wgsl) deliberately stay\n  perspective; ortho preview eyes are out of scope for #434.\n- Gate (Windows): the whole quick tier went green end to end at this\n  head on the first run after a boot - ui lib (338 unit tests) and\n  every ui integration suite, `trace_parity` 5/5 and `trace_composite`\n  4/4 included, under the lane's usual `--test-threads=6`; clippy\n  `-D warnings` green. On repeat runs minutes later those two\n  wgpu-heavy trace suites intermittently crash their process\n  (STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION, a different test each time) while\n  everything else stays green every run - it reproduces identically on\n  plain **main**, and both go green back-to-back serially, so it rides\n  no code here.\n\nChangelog: feat(viewport): parallel (orthographic) projection - the browser's Projection radios and bare P flip it; zoom, pan, orbit, frame and picks keep working (#434)\n\nFixes #434\n",
